        "captions": {
            "linkedin": "Deep work requires deep boundaries-even at home.\n\nI spent years building Digital Guardian because I understood this firsthand. My daughter is two now, and even at this age, I've learned that protecting focused time isn't just about my productivity. It's about modeling what healthy attention looks like.\n\nHere's what I've found through research from the University of Michigan's Center for Human Growth and Development:\n\nBoundaries aren't restrictive-they're generative. When I set clear parameters around my work time (and yes, screen-free playtime for my daughter), we both perform better. Her independent play builds executive function. My concentrated work sessions produce actual results-not just busywork.\n\nThe counterintuitive truth? Quality presence beats constant availability. A few hours of undivided attention trumps scattered moments throughout the day.\n\nWhat boundary would make your work-or your family life-better right now?\n\n\nFor more on balancing focus with family, follow along here.\n\n#DigitalGuardian #DigitalParenting #DigitalSafety #ParentingTips",
